  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 260-10-45-10, weighted-average shares reflect the time period during which shares were actually outstanding and available to earn income. Weighting by the fraction of the period each share was outstanding ensures EPS captures the actual capital base that generated earnings.
Wrong (A): Inflation in share price is irrelevant to the EPS computation; weighting is based on time outstanding, not price changes.
Wrong (C): Treasury stock reduces shares outstanding, but the purpose of weighting is to capture timing of share issuances and repurchases, not to adjust equity.
Wrong (D): The weighted-average requirement comes from ASC 260 (GAAP), not SEC market capitalization rules.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7653;

