Wrong (A): Although stock compensation is noncash, it is recognized in the income statement and reduces net income; it is not added back for EPS purposes.
Wrong (C): The options do affect diluted EPS beyond the expense; incremental shares from the treasury stock method increase the denominator.
Wrong (D): Stock compensation expense reduces net income, which decreases basic EPS; it does not increase EPS or reduce shares outstanding.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7661;

